---
components: ["Sparkline"]
description: Sparkline renders a small inline line or bar chart, sized to sit inside a stat tile alongside a label and value.
---

<script>
  import { Stack } from "carbon-components-svelte";
  import { Sparkline } from "carbon-components-svelte/viz";
</script>

`Sparkline` is part of the data visualization subpackage. Import it from `carbon-components-svelte/viz` and load `carbon-components-svelte/css/viz.css` alongside `all.css`. With a single-theme stylesheet such as `g100.css`, load the matching `viz-g100.css` instead. The subpackage is experimental: its API may change in a minor release.

## Basic

Create a sparkline with `values`, an array of numbers to plot. Set `label` to an accessible description of the series, such as "Requests per minute, last 24 hours", whenever the chart conveys information not stated elsewhere. Leave `label` empty to mark the chart as decorative.

<Sparkline values={[4, 7, 3, 9, 5, 12, 8, 6, 10, 14, 9, 13]} label="Requests per minute, last 24 hours" />

## Kinds

Set `kind` to `"line"` or `"bar"` to choose how the series is drawn.

### Line

<Sparkline values={[4, 7, 3, 9, 5, 12, 8, 6, 10, 14, 9, 13]} kind="line" />

### Bar

<Sparkline values={[4, 7, 3, 9, 5, 12, 8, 6, 10, 14, 9, 13]} kind="bar" />

## Colors

### Semantic

Set `color` to `"interactive"`, `"neutral"`, `"success"`, `"error"`, `"warning"`, or `"info"` to match the series to its meaning.

<Stack gap={5}>
  <Sparkline values={[4, 7, 3, 9, 5, 12, 8, 6, 10, 14, 9, 13]} color="interactive" />
  <Sparkline values={[4, 7, 3, 9, 5, 12, 8, 6, 10, 14, 9, 13]} color="neutral" />
  <Sparkline values={[4, 7, 3, 9, 5, 12, 8, 6, 10, 14, 9, 13]} color="success" />
  <Sparkline values={[4, 7, 3, 9, 5, 12, 8, 6, 10, 14, 9, 13]} color="error" />
  <Sparkline values={[4, 7, 3, 9, 5, 12, 8, 6, 10, 14, 9, 13]} color="warning" />
  <Sparkline values={[4, 7, 3, 9, 5, 12, 8, 6, 10, 14, 9, 13]} color="info" />
</Stack>

### Categorical

Set `color` to a number from 1 to 14 to use Carbon's categorical data visualization palette. The colors adapt to light and dark themes.

<Stack gap={5}>
  <Sparkline values={[4, 7, 3, 9, 5, 12, 8, 6, 10, 14, 9, 13]} color={1} />
  <Sparkline values={[9, 6, 11, 5, 8, 4, 7, 10, 6, 3, 8, 5]} color={2} />
  <Sparkline values={[2, 3, 5, 4, 6, 8, 7, 9, 11, 10, 12, 14]} color={3} />
</Stack>

### Custom

Any other string is used as a CSS color.

<Sparkline values={[4, 7, 3, 9, 5, 12, 8, 6, 10, 14, 9, 13]} color="rebeccapurple" />

## Missing values

A `null` or non-finite value is a gap. It keeps its slot, so the rest of the series stays aligned and two sparklines with different missing samples still line up.

<Stack gap={5}>
  <Sparkline values={[4, 7, 3, null, null, 12, 8, 6, 10, 14, 9, 13]} />
  <Sparkline values={[4, 7, 3, null, null, 12, 8, 6, 10, 14, 9, 13]} fill />
  <Sparkline values={[4, 7, 3, null, null, 12, 8, 6, 10, 14, 9, 13]} kind="bar" />
</Stack>

## Filled area

Set `fill` to `true` to shade the area under a line sparkline.

<Sparkline values={[4, 7, 3, 9, 5, 12, 8, 6, 10, 14, 9, 13]} kind="line" fill />

## Fixed domain

Set `min` and `max` to plot two sparklines against the same domain instead of each scaling to its own data, so their heights compare directly.

<Stack gap={5}>
  <Sparkline values={[2, 3, 4, 3, 5]} min={0} max={14} />
  <Sparkline values={[9, 11, 8, 12, 13]} min={0} max={14} />
</Stack>

## Sizing

Set `width` and `height` to change the viewBox dimensions. The svg also scales with a CSS width or height applied to it, since `preserveAspectRatio` is `"none"`.

<Sparkline values={[4, 7, 3, 9, 5, 12, 8, 6, 10, 14, 9, 13]} width={160} height={40} />
